<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As with the <span class="q5">legendary meta gem</span>, the cloak is a largely passive effect that correlates to approximately 4% of your damage on a single-target boss. However, unlike the meta gem, the cloak will cleave all targets in its range, making it very potent for AOE scenarios. <br/>
<br/>It operates on a Real Proc Per Minute (RPPM) system, meaning you are all but guaranteed to get a proc at the very beginning of the fight, then approximately 2 procs per minute. Additionally, it scales with Attack Power and can crit, but since we can't control the proc (except for the first hit of the encounter), we don't play around using cooldowns alongside the proc effect. <br/>
<br/>If you were thinking about using <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> for the cheat death effect, then this will unfortunately not be possible, as it does not function for non-tank specs.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Unholy Death Knight Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>As an Unholy Death Knight, you generally want trinkets that yield the highest amount of Strength possible, as this is your most precious Stat due to multiple modifiers.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Unholy Death Knights typically want two passive trinkets, as they can be used in conjunction with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a>, granting the highest amount of Strength possible. Since every single damage-dealing ability of a Death Knight scales with Strength, it is also your most desirable Stat by far. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105609/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> - This trinket is by far our best option for Phase 5, particularly as we approach full BIS. It amplifies our haste and mastery by 9% (when fully upgraded) and increases our critical strike damage by the same amount. On top of that, it also has a strength proc. This proc effect has an internal cooldown (ICD), unlike most other trinkets this tier.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105491/evil-eye-of-galakras">
<img alt="Evil Eye of Galakras" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Evil Eye of Galakras</span></a> - This trinket decreases the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=42650/army-of-the-dead">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_armyofthedead.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Army of the Dead</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49206/summon-gargoyle">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_summongargoyle.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Summon Gargoyle</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49016/unholy-frenzy">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unholyfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unholy Frenzy</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48792/icebound-fortitude">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_iceboundfortitude.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebound Fortitude</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48707/anti-magic-shell">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anti-Magic Shell</span></a> by up to 50% when fully upgraded. This is, of course, incredibly powerful, but one aspect often overlooked is the Runic Power generation value of the shorter cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48707/anti-magic-shell">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anti-Magic Shell</span></a>, particularly when combined with the new <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146648/glyph-of-regenerative-magic">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Regenerative Magic</span></a> for this phase.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is a very solid option if you're unable to get the aforementioned trinkets. Similarly to how you used <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=115989/unholy-blight">
